    "case_summary": "On routine screening, a 62-year-old man is found to have positive fecal occult blood tests. He is asymptomatic, but his father died of large intestinal cancer. Abdominal and rectal exams are normal. A colonoscopy subsequently reveals a polyp in the descending colon but no other abnormalities. Excisional biopsy of the polyp shows 75% tubular architecture. What is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. hyperplastic polyp\nB. tubular adenoma\nC. tubulovillous adenoma\nD. villous adenoma\nE. None\nF. None\nG. None\n",
